file docs-geode/libraries/README.md regenerated beside it
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the REDS pin will not accept another row and refused this one at the pre-commit wall, so the fold seat is now blocking rather than tidy: one word either folds an OPEN row or raises `living_pin_max_bytes` for REDS as was done once for the session-logs pin. Then -- the lane's next lap is orbit two's grant set, and it is agent-doable: declare the roughly nineteen mounts ai-jail supplies by default so the derivation reads a whole record rather than a sixth of one. Three seats want a word and none is mine: whether Pond should close the network at all once it owns the enclosure (the record now says HOLD out loud, which is the module asking); reds_fold.sh refusing OPEN rows, now blocking at 57 bytes rather than tidy; and this pier's own enclosure.conf, still pinning two elders under %327.
